      "message": "The walker changes look right to me: the `mm_pte_size()` stride, skipping repeats of the last swap entry, stopping at the next distinct entry and the `start_addr` alignment check all fit how reclaim fills the slice PTEs.\n\nCould the body say what goes wrong without the patch, though? \"This keeps per-process writeback and prefetch available for 4KB target processes\" reads as if they were refused before, which was only the case in earlier patch sets. Something like:\n\n```\nStepping by PAGE_SIZE reads one slice PTE per 16KB of a 4KB target,\nso a swapped-out page is missed when that slice is a hole, and a\nnext_addr in a VMA that isn\u0027t 16KB-aligned fails the start_addr check\nwhen it is passed back.\n```",
